# tcpdrill, what an unacceptable segment is answered with.
#
# RFC 793 3.9 page 69: an unacceptable segment is answered with an
# acknowledgment, unless it carries a RESET.  f7ca23ec narrowed that to segments
# from rx_sequence - 1 onwards, because an acknowledgment identical to the last
# one is counted as a duplicate ACK by the sender and three of those start a
# fast retransmit.  That reasoning holds for a segment carrying nothing and
# fails for one carrying data: the peer retransmitted because it never saw the
# acknowledgment, so the acknowledgment is the only thing that can stop it.
#
# THE THREE CASES ARE THE THREE ANSWERS.  d01 is a retransmission and must be
# acknowledged; d02 is an ancient acknowledgment and must draw nothing; d03 is a
# probe at rx_sequence - 1 and must be answered, which is what a keepalive and a
# zero-window probe both rely on.
#
# d01 restates o02_duplicate_segment from tcp.drill, so this file can be run on
# its own and the three answers read side by side.
#
# NONE OF THESE CASES HAS EVER BEEN RUN.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

# A hundred bytes, acknowledged, and sent again because the acknowledgment was
# lost.  Delivered once, acknowledged twice.
case d01_retransmitted_data_is_acknowledged_again
socket
connect
tx S seq=0
rx SA seq=0 ack=1 win=8192 mss=1460
tx A seq=1 ack=1
rx PA seq=1 ack=1 len=100
tx A seq=1 ack=101 within=400
rx PA seq=1 ack=1 len=100
tx A seq=1 ack=101 within=400
recv 400 = 100

# A bare acknowledgment from far behind the window carries nothing this side has
# not already answered, and answering it would be the duplicate ACK f7ca23ec
# measured.  Nothing goes out.
case d02_ancient_bare_ack_draws_nothing
socket
connect
tx S seq=0
rx SA seq=0 ack=1 win=8192 mss=1460
tx A seq=1 ack=1
rx PA seq=1 ack=1 len=100
tx A seq=1 ack=101 within=400
rx A seq=1 ack=1
notx 500

# One byte behind the window, which is where a keepalive and a zero-window probe
# both sit.  Drawing an acknowledgment out is their whole purpose, so this one is
# answered even though it carries nothing.
case d03_probe_at_the_left_edge_is_answered
socket
connect
tx S seq=0
rx SA seq=0 ack=1 win=8192 mss=1460
tx A seq=1 ack=1
rx PA seq=1 ack=1 len=100
tx A seq=1 ack=101 within=400
rx A seq=100 ack=1
tx A seq=1 ack=101 within=400
